{
  "planVersion": 1,
  "title": "Tags on posts",
  "summary": "Authors tag a post from a comma-separated field on the create and edit forms; the posts list and the post page show the tags, and a tag links to the list of posts carrying it.",
  "locale": "en",
  "scope": {
    "goals": [
      "Tag a post when creating or editing it, from one comma-separated field",
      "Show every post's tags on the posts list and the post page",
      "Filter the posts list by one tag with ?tag=<name>"
    ],
    "nonGoals": [
      "A page to rename, merge or delete tags",
      "Filtering by several tags at once",
      "Deleting tags no post uses any more"
    ]
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Names are trimmed and compared exactly (case-sensitive); empty entries between commas are ignored and duplicates collapse before the limit of 5 is counted.",
    "Leaving the field out or sending it empty saves the post with no tags.",
    "A post's tags are handed to pages sorted alphabetically by name.",
    "An unknown tag in ?tag= lists no posts and is not an error; the filtered list always starts on page 1 and its pagination links keep the tag.",
    "A tag no post uses any more stays in the tags table.",
    "Invalid tags fail the request exactly as an invalid title does (422 with errors on the tags field)."
  ],
